#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Action.md:82
msgid ""
"Returns: A short, localized name for the action at the specified `index`. "
"This is what screen readers will read out during normal navigation. For "
"example, \\\"Click\\\" for a button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Action.md:92
msgid "org.a11y.atspi.Action.GetKeyBinding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Action.md:96
msgid ""
"GetKeyBinding (\n"
"  IN index i,\n"
"  OUT unnamed_arg1 s\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Action.md:103
msgid ""
"Gets the keybinding which can be used to activate this action, if one "
"exists. The string returned should contain localized, human-readable, key "
"sequences as they would appear when displayed on screen. It must be in the "
"format \\\"mnemonic;sequence;shortcut\\\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Action.md:108
msgid ""
"The mnemonic key activates the object if it is presently enabled onscreen. "
"This typically corresponds to the underlined letter within the widget. "
"Example: \\\"n\\\" in a traditional \\\"New\\...\\\" menu item or the \\\"a\\"
"\" in \\\"Apply\\\" for a button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Action.md:112
msgid ""
"The sequence is the full list of keys which invoke the action even if the "
"relevant element is not currently shown on screen. For instance, for a menu "
"item the sequence is the keybindings used to open the parent menus before "
"invoking. The sequence string is colon-delimited. Example: \\\"Alt+F:N\\\" "
"in a traditional \\\"New\\...\\\" menu item."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Action.md:118
msgid ""
"The shortcut, if it exists, will invoke the same action without showing the "
"component or its enclosing menus or dialogs. Example: \\\"Ctrl+N\\\" in a "
"traditional \\\"New\\...\\\" menu item."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Action.md:122
msgid ""
"Example: For a traditional \\\"New\\...\\\" menu item, the expected return "
"value would be: \\\"N;Alt+F:N;Ctrl+N\\\" for the English locale and \\"
"\"N;Alt+D:N;Strg+N\\\" for the German locale. If, hypothetically, this menu "
"item lacked a mnemonic, it would be represented by \\\";;Ctrl+N\\\" and \\"
"\";;Strg+N\\\" respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Action.md:128
msgid "If there is no key binding for this action, return \\\"\\\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Action.md:136
msgid "org.a11y.atspi.Action.GetActions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Action.md:140
msgid ""
"GetActions (\n"
"  OUT unnamed_arg0 a(sss)\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Action.md:146
msgid ""
"Returns: an array of (localized_name, localized description, keybinding) for "
"the actions that an object supports. See the GetKeyBinding method for a "
"description of that field\\'s syntax."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Action.md:150
msgid ""
"This is equivalent to using the methods GetLocalizedName, GetDescription, "
"GetKeyBinding for each action, but with a single call and thus less D-Bus "
"traffic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Action.md:154
msgid ""
"By convention, if there is more than one action available, the first one is "
"considered the \\\"default\\\" action of the object."
msgstr ""

